# The image installs a clean, platform-correct dependency tree via `npm ci`;
# never copy a host node_modules (which may carry the wrong platform's native
# binaries) or local build output over it.
node_modules
.next
npm-debug.log*

# Playwright run artefacts, and the shared e2e session in particular. The
# Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything left on a developer's disk after an e2e
# run would otherwise be baked into an image layer — and `e2e/.auth/stylist.json`
# holds a LIVE Django session cookie. An image is a more durable and more
# portable artefact than the file itself: it survives `docker save`, layer
# inspection and any future registry push, all of which outlive the cookie's own
# intended lifecycle. The .gitignore entries close the git path and CI only
# uploads playwright-report/, so this is the third path and the one that is easy
# to forget. Baselines under e2e/*-snapshots/ are deliberately NOT excluded —
# they are committed reference images, not run output.
e2e/.auth
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.playwright
